    {
      "id": "b2",
      "function": "problem",
      "scene_type": "rv_plug",
      "spoken": "The insulator nose sits right in the fire. It has to get hot enough to burn off deposits by itself. According to NGK, a plug needs about four hundred and fifty degrees for that. If it runs too cold, deposits stay put.",
