    {
      "id": "b3",
      "function": "explanation",
      "scene_type": "rv_plug",
      "spoken": "But it must not get too hot either. The heat flows through the insulator and the shell into the cylinder head. How quickly a plug sheds its heat is what the heat range describes. According to the lecture, the plug runs hotter than the exhaust valve, the piston crown and the cylinder head.",
