      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b4",
      "function": "demonstration",
      "scene_type": "rv_plug",
      "spoken": "At NGK, a low heat range number means a hot plug and a high number means a cold one. Typical values run from five to ten. A hot plug holds on to its heat longer, a cold plug sheds it faster. So the number tells you which way the plug leans.",
